# acme_normal.wsp7 — P3 literal revision of the baseline sha256:00000000…0000, spec acme_normal-wsp-v7
# Author: claude-fable-5-2 (Anthropic). DATA-INFORMED, not zero-shot: every member is a data-informed
# candidate (see their own edits files for what each number was typed from).
#
#   slots c0, c1   acme_normal.wsp8 D1-EARLY, D1-LATE: the hinge law with the burner-heating law in
#                  place of its own burner-limit clock, for the early and the late era
#   slots c2, c3   the same two without their guessed stop times
#   slots b0, b1   acme_normal.wsp3 D3-EARLY, D3-LATE: the growth clock of each era
#   slots b2, b3   the same two without their guessed stop times
#   slots a0, a1   acme_normal.wsp2 D4 and D4-NOSTOPS, filled and silent here
#
# P3 is P2 with one change: the hinge member answers through the physical heating law of the burner
# instead of its own burner-limit clock. That clock is a log-logistic in fuel flow alone and gives a
# cool low-flow flame a limit trip it cannot have (21125A2 on TRAIN: a trip forecast at 17 s with
# the burner at 61 C; that one test is 16 % of P1's extinction loss on TRAIN). The heating law knows
# the total flow and the flame radius. Everything else is as in P2: the era by the date of the
# test, the planned stop after the stage sum, the three corrected statements.
#
# The slot values below were not typed again. They are the stored values of the releases named in
# the slot blocks, copied statement by statement by tools/wsp/committee2_edits.py with the slot
# prefix added. That script chooses and computes nothing. The lines typed for this file:

